A||||8||skitime||Did they give it to Dale Earnhardt Jr at Daytona?||||1||
Z||000000||skitime||07-07-2001||10:55 PM||||It seems that the drivers gave Dale Jr. the race tonight. No one would pass him till the big wreck and after the wreck they let him go to the lead.  Strange.  No flames please just an opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000001||kslish||07-08-2001||01:54 AM||||Dale Jr. clearly had the dominent car the entire race, the only one that could have probably had challenged in the end him was Waltrip (so yes, Waltrip maybe did let him have it). <P>Remember, everyone in front of him on the last two restarts had only taken on two tires, while Dale Jr, Waltrip and some others in the back had four fresh tires.  Benson (leader on the restart) was simply a sitting duck with only two tires, I bet he would have been a lot more aggressive if he had all new tires under him (since he was racing for his first Winston Cup win).  <P>Add that to the fact that Dale Jr's car probably had 20hp on the entire field since his team had obviously sacrificed fuel economy for power....a gamble that paid off since there were cautions.  He was running about 5 laps less per tank (about 50 laps per stop instead of 55) than most others in the field.  If it went green all the way, he would have been out of luck because he would have had to make one more stop for fuel than probably most everyone else in the field.  <P>I did feel bad for Harvick, since he seemed to have an awesome car too (he could come up through the pack with ease) but he got caught in the wrong place at the right time.  It must have sucked to just be slowing down to come in for your last pit stop when suddenly there are 10 cars going sideways in front of you in the entrance to pit lane.  There was simply noplace for him to go.  I was looking forward to maybe him and Dale Jr. going at it in the end.<P>I also wonder if Nascar will really penalize Tony Stewart for going below the yellow line near the end.  They did show him the black flag, but when they showed the replay, he clearly was forced down there by Benson blocking him, who was fading fast after the restart.  Would the Nascar officials have preferred it if Stewart kept his line and rear ended Benson, causing yet another wreck right before the finish?<P>Ken S.<p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 07-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Galen||07-08-2001||05:32 AM||||They shouldn't penalize him for it. If they do, its bad on their part. Oh well. Who cares? Dale Jr rocked! an Waltrip showed a LOT of class there. I simply love it. I was a Big E fan since a couple years ago after Ernie Irvan retired. The Earnhardt Legacy at Daytona continues.. No matter how fubar'ed the world gets, a Carolina boy can show exactly whats right in the world. Ya gotta love it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/boyandpc.gif"> <BR>"To whom it may concern, The preceeding message was the opinion of this person and not of this forum. If you do not like it. Oh well"||||reg||1
